{"id":"9f5e874a-61d3-4ced-bd04-c3bb9013652c","object":"chat.completion","created":1789627532,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"schema\":\"amr-supervisor/v1\",\"select\":[{\"when\":\"OwnerFree and RequestA\",\"action\":\"SelectA\"},{\"when\":\"OwnerFree and RequestB\",\"action\":\"SelectB\"},{\"when\":\"True\",\"action\":\"Defer\"}],\"step\":[{\"when\":\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"Stopped\"},{\"when\":\"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},{\"when\":\"AtGoal and Released and Halted\",\"action\":\"Finish\",\"next\":\"Done\"},{\"when\":\"AtGoal and Released\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},{\"when\":\"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\",\"action\":\"Release\",\"next\":\"Traversing\"},{\"when\":\"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},{\"when\":\"not OwnReservation and not Released\",\"action\":\"Request\",\"next\":\"Waiting\"},{\"when\":\"ModeStopped\",\"action\":\"Resume\",\"next\":\"ResumePending\"},{\"when\":\"True\",\"action\":\"Proceed\",\"next\":\"Traversing\"}]}","reasoning_content":"We need answer only JSON. Need solve. Need produce complete program satisfying spec. Need carefully synthesize select and step rules.\n\nWe have feedback from previous candidate. Need revise. Let's parse requirements.\n\nWe need JSON schema \"amr-supervisor/v1\", select array <=12 rules, step array <=12 rules. Total branches <=32 (rules count) per function <=12. Expressions allowed booleans names etc.\n\nSelect:\nInputs OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB, PreferA, PreferB. Actions SelectA requires OwnerFree and RequestA. SelectB requires OwnerFree and RequestB. If reservation free and at least one request exists, select eligible robot, rather than Defer. Otherwise Defer required. When both eligible, either legal; preferences advisory.\n\nNeed total. Simple:\n1 when OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA (if both, selects A)\n2 when OwnerFree and RequestB -> SelectB\n3 True -> Defer\nThis satisfies: if OwnerFree true and RequestA true but RequestB false select A. If both true select A (allowed). If only B select B. If no request or not OwnerFree Defer. Preference irrelevant. Need maybe if OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB choose either, SelectA okay. Fine.\n\nStep: Need encode policy priority. Need be very careful.\n\nInputs: ObservationUsable, PedestrianBlocked, OwnReservation, Released, BodyClearOfZ, Halted, AtGoal, TaskActive.\nModes: one-hot ModeIdle, ModeWaiting, ModeTraversing, ModeBrakeRequested, ModeStopped, ModeResumePending, ModeDone.\nActions: Request, Proceed, Brake, Resume, Release, Finish. Each rule action and next mode explicit.\n\nPolicy:\nOrdinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by following requirements. Authority from highest to lowest:\n1 invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling\n2 released-goal handling\n3 whole-body release\n4 unfinished braking\n5 reservation request\n6 restart transition\n7 ordinary motion\n\nNeed interpret \"released-goal handling\" highest after invalid: AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish enter Done.\n\n\"whole-body release\": OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking considered. (Authority 3)\n\n\"unfinished braking\": BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; overrides missing-reservation request. But note mode? Wording \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" likely current mode BrakeRequested? It says \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested\". The earlier \"The restart transition applies to current Stopped mode...\" Maybe \"BrakeRequested\" here refers current mode ModeBrakeRequested? The previous candidate had ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. Feedback did not flag? Need infer. Inputs include Halted. Policy: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request. However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" It likely means current mode BrakeRequested (ModeBrakeRequested) and not Halted. Since \"unfinished braking\" applies in BrakeRequested mode. Need encode rule: ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake, BrakeRequested. What if current mode BrakeRequested but Halted true? Then unfinished braking no longer, lower rules apply. But invalid/goal etc higher. Missing reservation? If not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request Waiting overrides restart transition but lower than braking. If current BrakeRequested and Halted true, no braking; missing reservation if neither own nor released -> Request Waiting. If OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing. If stopped and etc.\n\n\"reservation request\": A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides restart transition. So rule: not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request, Waiting. This applies all modes except if higher (invalid, goal, release, unfinished braking). Important: If mode Stopped and missing reservation, Request Waiting overrides restart. If mode Idle and missing reservation, Request Waiting rather than Proceed. If mode Done? Policy applies every mode. But if Done and missing reservation? Then Request Waiting unless higher? Need yes: all modes. However AtGoal/Released might be true? If Done and AtGoal Released and Halted -> Finish Done (higher). If not released etc maybe Request. Need follow literal.\n\n\"restart transition\": applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request... overrides restart. So rule after missing reservation: ModeStopped -> Resume ResumePending. But also if OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ higher -> Release Traversing. If BrakeRequested without Halted higher if mode? Not relevant if mode Stopped. Invalid/goal higher. So okay.\n\n\"ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing.\" This last default, applies all remaining. Need ensure total. So default True -> Proceed Traversing. But need account if rule order handles all.\n\nHighest invalid/blocked/task-inactive:\nWhenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\nSo need two rules:\n1 when (not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted -> Brake, Stopped\n2 when not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked -> Brake, BrakeRequested\nOrder within same condition: Halted first. In previous candidate had non-Halted rule first? It had:\n{\"when\":\"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"Stopped\"},\n{\"when\":\"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},\nThis is wrong: first doesn't include Halted, so always Stopped even when Halted false. Feedback flagged. Need fix: include Halted in first, then fallback.\n\nThen released-goal:\nAtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish Done\nAtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested (or simply AtGoal and Released after Halted rule)\nNeed priority after invalid. Order:\n3 when AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish Done\n4 when AtGoal and Released -> Brake BrakeRequested\nIf AtGoal Released true and invalid false (since invalid rule above), okay. If Halted true, Finish. If Halted false, Brake. Does \"without Halted\" for Brake, \"with Halted\" Finish. Yes.\n\nWhole-body release:\nOwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing. Is this higher than unfinished braking. Need maybe if AtGoal&Released and OwnReservation&BodyClearOfZ, goal higher, so goal rules above. Invalid above. Good. Should this require mode? No, policy says OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing. It applies all modes, even Done? It says before unfinished braking. No other condition. So rule:\n5 when OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing\nBut consider Halted? If OwnReservation BodyClearOfZ true and Halted false etc. Release. If current mode BrakeRequested and not Halted, but OwnReservation BodyClear true, Release higher. Yes.\n\nUnfinished braking:\nModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested. But what if current mode is something else? \"BrakeRequested without Halted\" maybe could mean action? The input doesn't include action. It likely uses mode flag. Need use ModeBrakeRequested. Need perhaps \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\" after release. If Halted true, no brake. Good.\n\nReservation request:\nnot OwnReservation and not Released -> Request Waiting. This overrides restart transition. Need order after unfinished braking, before restart. Consider if mode BrakeRequested and not Halted: brake above, so no request even if missing reservation. Policy says unfinished braking overrides missing-reservation request. If mode BrakeRequested and Halted true, then request if missing. That seems plausible.\nHowever, what if OwnReservation false, Released false, but invalid/goal/release? release requires OwnReservation so no; goal higher. invalid higher. okay.\n\nRestart transition:\nModeStopped -> Resume ResumePending. Need after missing reservation. But careful: if mode Stopped and OwnReservation&BodyClear -> Release above. If missing reservation -> Request above. If AtGoal&Released -> goal above. If invalid -> brake. If BrakeRequested? not Stopped. Good.\n\nOrdinary motion:\nTrue -> Proceed Traversing. Need after restart. That gives default.\n\nNeed verify all 1792 combos. Need ensure rule list covers all and order priority. But possible issue: \"unfinished braking\" maybe not only current mode BrakeRequested; also if Halted false and something? The phrase \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested\" might refer current mode BrakeRequested. Yes.\n\nNeed consider priority hierarchy and rule interactions with Halted. Let's formalize.\n\nRules:\n0 invalid & Halted -> Brake Stopped\n1 invalid -> Brake BrakeRequested\n2 AtGoal & Released & Halted -> Finish Done\n3 AtGoal & Released -> Brake BrakeRequested\n4 OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ -> Release Traversing\n5 ModeBrakeRequested & not Halted -> Brake BrakeRequested\n6 not OwnReservation & not Released -> Request Waiting\n7 ModeStopped -> Resume ResumePending\n8 True -> Proceed Traversing\n\nThat's 9 rules. Need check if any missing higher conditions: AtGoal and Released with Halted true -> Finish. What if AtGoal and Released false? Lower. Goal handling only if both true. If AtGoal true, Released false, maybe missing reservation -> Request if neither; or release if OwnReservation BodyClear; or stop if invalid. Is that policy? \"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true...\" yes only both. AtGoal alone not special. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"released-goal handling\" authority 2: AtGoal and Released both true. If Halted true, Finish Done. If Halted false, Brake BrakeRequested. Our rule 3 AtGoal & Released (not Halted?) after Halted rule. Since if Halted true, rule 2 catches. If Halted false, rule3 catches. If Halted true but invalid also true, invalid higher catches. yes.\n\nPotential issue: invalid rule with Halted: \"Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise.\" If invalid and Halted true -> Brake Stopped. Good. If invalid and Halted false -> Brake BrakeRequested. Good. What if invalid and AtGoal Released Halted true? invalid higher -> Brake Stopped, not Finish. Good.\n\nPotential issue: whole-body release rule after goal. Suppose AtGoal Released Halted true and OwnReservation BodyClear true. Goal higher -> Finish Done. Suppose AtGoal Released false and OwnReservation BodyClear true. Release. Is that correct? Policy says released-goal handling higher than whole-body release, but only AtGoal&Released both true. If Released false, no goal handling, release applies. That means even if AtGoal true but not Released, and own body clear, Release Traversing. Is that intended? Literal: \"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true...\" \"The ordinary... displaced by following requirements... whole-body release: OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release...\" Yes, if AtGoal true but Released false, release if own+body. Although weird maybe if at goal but not released, should release? Released = acknowledged reservation release for task; BodyClear = whole body clear of controlled zone. If at goal but not released, maybe still own reservation and clear, release? It says requirement. Okay.\n\nPotential issue: reservation request \"when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true\"; our condition not OwnReservation and not Released. Good. If Released true and OwnReservation false, missing reservation? No, Released true so not request. Then if mode Stopped -> Resume, or default Proceed. Is that correct? \"missing reservation requires Request ... when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true.\" So Released true counts as not missing? Yes distinct. If Released true and not OwnReservation, no request. Then if mode BrakeRequested and not Halted -> brake above; if mode Stopped -> restart Resume; else Proceed. Could that be physically odd but per rules.\n\nPotential issue: \"unfinished braking\" authority 4: BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides missing-reservation request. But if current mode BrakeRequested and Halted true, no unfinished braking. Then missing reservation could apply. If own/reservation/released? If neither, Request Waiting. If OwnReservation and BodyClear, Release higher. If released and at goal etc. If Halted true and BrakeRequested, maybe should Stop? Policy doesn't say. If invalid and Halted true -> Brake Stopped above. If no invalid, not goal, not release, not unfinished because Halted, then missing reservation -> Request Waiting, or if has reservation/released then default Proceed Traversing? Wait if current mode BrakeRequested and Halted true, but no missing reservation, no restart (not Stopped), then default Proceed Traversing. Is that intended? Let's examine. BrakeRequested mode with Halted true: The robot has completed braking (trusted stop confirmation). What should happen next? Policy hierarchy: invalid handling, goal, release, unfinished braking, missing reservation, restart transition, ordinary motion. There is no explicit \"if BrakeRequested and Halted then ...\" except unfinished braking applies only without Halted. If Halted true, maybe proceed? But if robot halted and task active, observation usable, no pedestrian, not at goal/released, own reservation maybe true, body clear maybe? If BodyClearOfZ true and OwnReservation true, release rule would fire (Release Traversing). If not, maybe missing reservation? If OwnReservation true, no request. Then default Proceed Traversing even though halted. This is what ordered rules say. Could be okay.\n\nPotential issue: \"restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending.\" It doesn't say require Halted? Current Stopped means mode. Rule ModeStopped -> Resume. But what if missing reservation? Request above. What if invalid? Brake above. If AtGoal Released? Finish or Brake above. If OwnReservation BodyClear? Release above. If ModeStopped and Halted? Resume. If ModeStopped and not Halted? Resume if no higher. Is that intended? The policy says restart transition applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume. It doesn't condition on Halted. But Stopped mode likely implies Halted? They say don't infer relationships. So yes, ModeStopped alone triggers Resume unless higher. Previous candidate had that. Feedback did not flag. But consider invalid with ModeStopped and Halted true: highest invalid -> Brake Stopped. Good. If invalid and ModeStopped Halted false: Brake BrakeRequested. Good. If missing reservation and ModeStopped: Request Waiting overrides restart. Good.\n\nPotential issue: In invalid rule, entering Stopped if Halted true and BrakeRequested otherwise. If already ModeStopped and invalid Halted true, action Brake next Stopped. That's allowed? Policy says return Brake; enter Stopped if Halted true. Yes.\n\nNeed ensure expressions syntax allowed. Use names exactly. Parentheses optional. Python Boolean precedence: not > and > or. We can write:\n\"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked and Halted\"? Careful precedence. Need parenthesize for invalid & Halted. Use parentheses: \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\". Allowed parentheses. condition length okay. 64 AST nodes? Let's count: \"not ObservationUsable\" (UnaryOp, Name) etc. Parentheses. Under 64. Depth <8 maybe: or(and) depth? For first: (not O or not T or P) and H -> depth: BoolOp And -> BoolOp Or -> UnaryOp -> Name = 4. okay.\n\nSecond invalid: \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\" depth 3.\n\nAtGoal and Released and Halted depth 3.\nAtGoal and Released depth 2.\nOwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ depth 2.\nModeBrakeRequested and not Halted depth 3.\nnot OwnReservation and not Released: Python precedence: not > and. Expression \"not OwnReservation and not Released\" means (not OwnReservation) and (not Released). Good. depth 3.\nModeStopped depth 1.\nTrue depth 1.\n\nNeed select. Could include preferences? Not needed. But maybe select requires if OwnerFree and at least one request exists, select eligible robot rather than Defer. If both eligible, either legal. Our select: if OwnerFree and RequestA -> SelectA; if OwnerFree and RequestB -> SelectB; else Defer. What if OwnerFree true, RequestA true, RequestB true: SelectA. What if OwnerFree true, RequestA false, RequestB true: SelectB. What if OwnerFree false but RequestA true: first false, second maybe false if RequestB false, then Defer. If OwnerFree false, RequestB true: second false due OwnerFree, Defer. Good. If OwnerFree true, RequestA false, RequestB false: Defer. If OwnerFree true, RequestA true, RequestB true: SelectA. Legal. Preferences ignored. Good.\n\nNeed consider total branches <=32. Select 3 rules, step 9 rules total 12 branches. Per function okay. Source <200KB.\n\nBut we need make sure previous candidate rejected due source/model mismatch. Our step list fix invalid Halted. But wait previous candidate also had no default Proceed? Actually previous candidate had 8 rules, no True default. Feedback example: step Idle AtGoal false BodyClear false Halted false ObservationUsable true OwnReservation false Pedestrian false Released true TaskActive true expected Proceed Traversing. Previous source no matching because no default. Our default fixes. Also previous invalid rule wrong. Need ensure all other requirements.\n\nLet's deeply analyze policy and possible hidden issues. We need produce accepted by independent model. Let's derive exact model from policy.\n\nGiven feedback mentions \"allowed_outputs\": [[\"Proceed\",\"Traversing\"]] for Idle with Released true, OwnReservation false, AtGoal false, BodyClear false, Halted false, Observation true, Pedestrian false, TaskActive true. In our rules:\n0 invalid & Halted? invalid false.\n1 invalid false.\n2 AtGoal Released Halted false.\n3 AtGoal false.\n4 OwnReservation false.\n5 ModeBrakeRequested? mode Idle false.\n6 not OwnReservation and not Released: Released true -> false.\n7 ModeStopped false.\n8 True -> Proceed Traversing. Good.\n\nAnother example invalid false? Feedback actual previous [\"Brake\",\"Stopped\"] allowed [[\"Brake\",\"BrakeRequested\"]] for ObservationUsable false, TaskActive false, Halted false. Our rule 0: invalid & Halted false. rule1 invalid -> Brake BrakeRequested. Good.\n\nNeed maybe there are hidden defects beyond displayed. Let's consider all policy nuances. The feedback says previous had 55 correspondence mismatches, 839 model violations, source violations. We need full acceptance. Let's reconstruct model and compare.\n\nPotential tricky: \"The ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by the following requirements. Their authority, from highest to lowest, is: invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling; released-goal handling; whole-body release; unfinished braking; reservation request; restart transition; ordinary motion.\"\n\nThis is a priority list. We order rules high to low. Need ensure each requirement's conditions exactly as specified. Let's parse each.\n\n1 invalid/blocked/task-inactive handling:\n\"Highest of all, whenever ObservationUsable is false, TaskActive is false, or PedestrianBlocked is true, return Brake. Under that highest-priority condition, enter Stopped if Halted is true and BrakeRequested otherwise. Thus even an arrived and halted robot must obey this highest-priority rule if its input is blocked or invalid.\"\n\nCondition: not ObservationUsable OR not TaskActive OR PedestrianBlocked. Action Brake. Next: if Halted then Stopped else BrakeRequested. So two rules. Good. Note PedestrianBlocked true regardless TaskActive? yes. Halted determines next.\n\n2 released-goal handling:\n\"Higher than all these is arrival with AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\"\nCondition: AtGoal AND Released. If Halted true -> Finish Done; if false -> Brake BrakeRequested. But priority after invalid, so if invalid true, invalid applies. Our rules: AtGoal Released Halted -> Finish Done; AtGoal Released -> Brake BrakeRequested. Since second catches Halted false because first false. If Halted true and AtGoal Released true, first. Good.\n\n3 whole-body release:\n\"However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\"\nCondition: OwnReservation AND BodyClearOfZ. Action Release next Traversing. No Halted condition. Our rule 4 after goal. Good.\n\n4 unfinished braking:\n\"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\"\nCondition: current mode BrakeRequested? The text uses \"BrakeRequested\" as mode. \"unfinished braking\" likely ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. Action Brake next BrakeRequested. Our rule 5. Good.\nBut wait, what if current mode is BrakeRequested and Halted true? The condition \"without Halted\" false. So no. But if current mode BrakeRequested and Halted false, rule applies even if OwnReservation and BodyClear? Whole-body release higher, so release first. Good.\n\n5 reservation request:\n\"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\"\nCondition: not OwnReservation AND not Released. Action Request next Waiting. Our rule 6. Good.\nPotential subtlety: \"missing reservation\" might apply only if TaskActive? No, if TaskActive false, invalid higher. So if task inactive, invalid. If Observation invalid, invalid. Pedestrian, invalid. So lower not matter.\nPotential subtlety: Should this apply in every mode including Done? Policy says apply every input combination and mode. So yes. Our rule applies any mode. If ModeDone and not own and not released, request Waiting (unless higher). Is that intended? The policy says no special terminal-mode shortcut, requirements apply in every mode including Done. So yes. If ModeDone and missing reservation, Request Waiting. That might be weird but required.\n\n6 restart transition:\n\"The restart transition applies to a current Stopped mode and yields Resume, entering ResumePending. A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\"\nCondition: ModeStopped. Action Resume next ResumePending. Our rule 7 after reservation request. Good.\nPotential subtlety: Should restart transition only if Halted? It says current Stopped mode. No.\n\n7 ordinary motion:\n\"ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing.\" Default. Our rule 8 True -> Proceed Traversing.\n\nThus 9 rules. Should satisfy.\n\nBut let's think about interaction: If ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted and invalid false, AtGoal Released true? Released-goal higher. Suppose AtGoal Released true, Halted false, ModeBrakeRequested. Priority: invalid no, released-goal yes -> Brake BrakeRequested. Our rule 3 catches before rule5. Action same as unfinished braking but next same. If Halted true, rule2 Finish Done before rule5. But mode BrakeRequested Halted true; released-goal says Finish Done. Is that correct? Priority says released-goal higher than unfinished braking. Yes.\n\nSuppose OwnReservation BodyClear true, ModeBrakeRequested not Halted. Priority: whole-body release higher than unfinished braking. Our rule 4 Release Traversing before rule5. Good. Is that intended? \"However, OwnReservation together with BodyClearOfZ requires Release, entering Traversing, before unfinished braking is considered.\" Yes.\n\nSuppose ModeStopped and not OwnReservation not Released. Reservation request higher than restart. Our rule6 Request Waiting before rule7. Good.\n\nSuppose ModeStopped and invalid false, AtGoal Released true, Halted true. Released-goal higher than restart. Our rule2 Finish Done. Good.\nSuppose ModeStopped and OwnReservation BodyClear true. Whole-body release higher than restart. Rule4 Release Traversing. Good.\n\nNow, could there be any issue with \"AtGoal and Released both true: without Halted, return Brake and enter BrakeRequested; with Halted, return Finish and enter Done.\" If Halted true but invalid false, we Finish. If Halted false, Brake. Our second rule \"AtGoal and Released\" catches Halted false only because Halted true caught above. But what if Halted is not a Boolean? It's Boolean. Fine.\n\nNow, the feedback says \"At most 32 total branches are allowed; per-function limit twelve still applies.\" We have 12 total. Good.\n\nNeed produce exactly JSON no markdown. Ensure valid JSON. Use double quotes. No comments.\n\nLet's ensure no duplicate keys. Keys: schema, select, step. Each rule has when, action, next for step. Select rules have when, action only. Need not include next for select.\n\nLet's craft final JSON:\n\n{\n  \"schema\": \"amr-supervisor/v1\",\n  \"select\": [\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestA\", \"action\": \"SelectA\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestB\", \"action\": \"SelectB\"},\n    {\"when\": \"True\", \"action\": \"Defer\"}\n  ],\n  \"step\": [\n    {\"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"Stopped\"},\n    {\"when\": \"not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\", \"action\": \"Finish\", \"next\": \"Done\"},\n    {\"when\": \"AtGoal and Released\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\", \"action\": \"Release\", \"next\": \"Traversing\"},\n    {\"when\": \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"not OwnReservation and not Released\", \"action\": \"Request\", \"next\": \"Waiting\"},\n    {\"when\": \"ModeStopped\", \"action\": \"Resume\", \"next\": \"ResumePending\"},\n    {\"when\": \"True\", \"action\": \"Proceed\", \"next\": \"Traversing\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nCheck condition \"not OwnReservation and not Released\" Python precedence: not binds tighter than and, so (not OwnReservation) and (not Released). Good.\n\nBut wait: In step, \"ModeBrakeRequested\" is permitted name. Exactly one mode flag true. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: The policy says \"The ordinary step outcome is Proceed, entering Traversing. It is displaced by the following requirements.\" In our rule 7 ModeStopped -> Resume before default. But what about ModeStopped and Halted false, no missing reservation, no own/reserve? It resumes. The restart transition applies to current Stopped mode and yields Resume. It doesn't say only if Halted. Good.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"A missing reservation requires Request, entering Waiting, when neither OwnReservation nor Released is true; this overrides the restart transition.\" Suppose OwnReservation false, Released true. Not missing. So if ModeStopped, restart applies -> Resume. Is that correct? If Released true but OwnReservation false, the reservation has been released. Should robot resume? Policy says Released distinct from BodyClear. Missing reservation if neither OwnReservation nor Released. Since Released true, no request. Then restart transition applies. So yes.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"unfinished braking\" condition might include Halted false universally, not mode? Let's examine wording: \"BrakeRequested without Halted must continue Brake, entering BrakeRequested; this overrides a missing-reservation request.\" It could be interpreted as: if the action/mode is BrakeRequested (i.e., a Brake has been requested and not halted), continue Brake. The only way to know is ModeBrakeRequested. Yes.\n\nPotential hidden issue: What if current mode is not BrakeRequested but Halted false and OwnReservation false Released false? Reservation request -> Request Waiting. But if the robot had previously issued Brake? Not represented except mode. So okay.\n\nPotential hidden issue: \"invalid/blocked/task-in